{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-07-21T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some structures weren't meant to stand out—but time had other ideas. At sunrise, the Santa Catalina Arch glows over the streets of Antigua, Guatemala, its yellow facade catching the light just right as cobblestones stretch ahead and Agua Volcano rises in the distance. The arch was built in the 17th century to solve a practical problem: cloistered nuns needed to cross between convent buildings without being seen from the street. Privacy, not postcards, created one of Central America's most photographed landmarks. Irony holds up well over time.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatalina_EN-IN9392067972_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SantaCatalina_EN-IN9392067972_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Hidden in plain arch","Title":"Santa Catalina Arch, Antigua, Guatemala","Copyright":"© Filippo Maria Bianchi/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/14.559567,-90.73426/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=14.559567,-90.73426;S9;Santa Catalina Arch, Antigua, Sacatepéquez, Guatemala&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260721_SantaCatalina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Santa+Catalina+Arch+Guatemala&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260720_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260721_SantaCatalina"},"Ssd":"20260721","Name":"SantaCatalina","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9392067972","FullDateString":"21 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From the moon's cratered surface, Earth appears as a thin, glowing crescent against the darkness—a rare view that reverses our usual perspective. This stark landscape, shaped by billions of years of impacts, preserves a record of the early solar system. 20 July marks International Moon Day, commemorating the 1969 Apollo 11 landing, when humans first set foot on the lunar surface. Established by the United Nations in 2021, the day highlights past achievements and ongoing efforts to explore the moon.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Artemis_EN-IN9018589977_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Artemis_EN-IN9018589977_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The lunar perspective","Title":"Moon and Earth captured by the Artemis II crew","Copyright":"© NASA","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The moon rotates at the same rate it orbits Earth, so we always see the same side from our planet.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260720_Artemis\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Moon+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260719_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260720_Artemis"},"Ssd":"20260720","Name":"Artemis","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9018589977","FullDateString":"20 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Perched on slender reeds, a group of barn swallows gathers in a moment of stillness that contrasts with their usual speed. Known for swift, acrobatic flight and deeply forked tails, these birds are built for life on the wing. They catch insects mid-air and travel vast distances between continents. Subtle variations in colour and markings suggest that more than one subspecies may be present, reflecting the barn swallow's extensive global range.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HirundoRustica_EN-IN8751353148_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HirundoRustica_EN-IN8751353148_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Wings at rest","Title":"Barn swallows of different subspecies resting together","Copyright":"© Oscar Dominguez/Tandem Stills + Motion","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Barn swallows can travel thousands of miles between their breeding and wintering grounds each year.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260719_HirundoRustica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Barn+swallow&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260718_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260719_HirundoRustica"},"Ssd":"20260719","Name":"HirundoRustica","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8751353148","FullDateString":"19 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Reflected in still water, the Rakotzbrücke—commonly known as the Devil's Bridge—forms a near-perfect stone circle in Saxony, Germany. Commissioned in 1860, the narrow basalt structure was carefully engineered so that its arch and reflection align to form a seamless ring when the lake is still. Made from locally sourced volcanic stone, it reflects precise design rather than practical function, its striking geometry intended purely for visual effect. A popular photo subject, it has also appeared in films, including 'The Matrix Resurrections' (2021). Today, the fragile bridge can only be admired from the shore, as crossing is prohibited to preserve it.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DevilsBridge_EN-IN8517892146_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DevilsBridge_EN-IN8517892146_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Going full circle","Title":"Devil's Bridge in Rhododendron Park Kromlau, Saxony, Germany","Copyright":"© Mike Mareen/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/51.53661,14.640453/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=51.53661,14.640453;S9;Devil's Bridge, Kromlau, Saxony, Germany&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260718_DevilsBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Devils+Bridge+Kromlau&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260717_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260718_DevilsBridge"},"Ssd":"20260718","Name":"DevilsBridge","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8517892146","FullDateString":"18 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On the remote northeastern tip of Crete, Greece, lies a quiet corner far from typical tourist routes. Today's image shows Vai Beach, a broad curve of golden sand bordered by calm, shallow waters of the Aegean Sea. With sunbeds, umbrellas, and showers, it's ideal for swimming, relaxing, or enjoying the peaceful atmosphere. But what truly sets Vai apart is just beyond the sand: Europe's largest natural palm grove. It consists of more than 5,000 Cretan date palm trees, a species native to Crete and parts of Turkey.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VaiUmbrellas_EN-IN8171582034_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VaiUmbrellas_EN-IN8171582034_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A Greek escape","Title":"Blue sunbeds on a sandy beach in Vai, Crete, Greece","Copyright":"© borchee/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.30972,24.89333/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.30972,24.89333;S9;Crete, Greece&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":"/maps?ty=30&q=crete%20greece&satid=id.sid%3Aa898a116-f402-c866-449a-1e49d7c0585b&vdpid=7247538364818128897&mb=36.013862~23.514471~34.598793~26.318979&cardbg=%23F98745&dt=1749198600000&tt=Crete%2C%20Crete%2C%20Greece&tsts0=%2526ty%253D30%2526q%253Dcrete%252520greece%2526satid%253Did.sid%25253Aa898a116-f402-c866-449a-1e49d7c0585b%2526vdpid%253D7247538364818128897%2526mb%253D36.013862~23.514471~34.598793~26.318979%2526cardbg%253D%252523F98745%2526dt%253D1749198600000&tstt0=Crete%2C%20Crete%2C%20Greece&cp=34.85975~13.56328&lvl=4.98&pi=0&ftst=0&ftics=False&v=2&sV=2&form=hpbal1"},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260717_VaiUmbrellas\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Crete+Greece&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260716_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260717_VaiUmbrellas"},"Ssd":"20260717","Name":"VaiUmbrellas","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8171582034","FullDateString":"17 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As Rath Yatra begins today, Puri, Odisha, will once again become the stage for one of India's most celebrated traditions. The festival sees Lord Jagannath, his brother Balabhadra and his sister Subhadra pulled through the streets on towering wooden chariots. The deities travel about 3 kilometres from the Jagannath Temple to Gundicha Temple, believed to be their aunt's home, where they stay for nine days.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RathYatra2026_EN-IN7824400350_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RathYatra2026_EN-IN7824400350_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The wheels of tradition","Title":"The Stone Chariot, Hampi, Karnataka","Copyright":"© Alan_Lagadu/iStock/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/15.342253,76.475837/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=15.342253,76.475837;S9;The Stone Chariot, Hampi, Karnataka&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260716_RathYatra2026\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rath+Yatra&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260715_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260716_RathYatra2026"},"Ssd":"20260716","Name":"RathYatra2026","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7824400350","FullDateString":"16 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"If mountains could keep a record of the past, the John Muir Wilderness near Bishop, California, United States, would have plenty to share. Its valleys, lakes and granite formations reveal a history shaped over millions of years. Established in 1964, this vast protected area spans more than 2,600 square kilometres of the Sierra Nevada and is named after naturalist John Muir. Today, parts of the Pacific Crest Trail and John Muir Trail pass through the area, drawing hikers into one of the largest high-elevation wilderness regions in the contiguous United States.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.MarieLake_EN-IN7488025421_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.MarieLake_EN-IN7488025421_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"The reward after the climb","Title":"Marie Lake, John Muir Wilderness near Bishop, California, United States","Copyright":"© Steve Dunleavy/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/36.97615,-118.812278/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=36.97615,-118.812278;S9;John Muir Wilderness, California, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260715_MarieLake\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=John+Muir+Wilderness&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260714_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260715_MarieLake"},"Ssd":"20260715","Name":"MarieLake","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7488025421","FullDateString":"15 Jul, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Off Anacapa Island, California, United States, the ocean grows its own forests. Within Channel Islands National Park—also known as the 'Galápagos of North America'—giant kelp stretches beyond 30 metres in length, forming buoyant ribbons lifted by air-filled bladders and anchored below by rootlike holdfasts.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ChannelKelp_EN-IN9944710575_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ChannelKelp_EN-IN9944710575_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A balance in motion","Title":"A kelp forest off Anacapa Island, Channel Islands National Park, California, United States","Copyright":"© Ian Shive/Tandem Stills + Motion","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/34.004342,-119.391995/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=34.004342,-119.391995;S9;Anacapa Island, California, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260728_ChannelKelp\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=World+Nature+Conservation+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260727_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260728_ChannelKelp"},"Ssd":"20260728","Name":"ChannelKelp","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9944710575","FullDateString":"28 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Step inside the Chicago Cultural Center in Illinois, United States, and your eyes are instantly drawn upwards to a glowing canopy of colour—the Tiffany Dome. Suspended above Preston Bradley Hall, this masterpiece spans over 11 metres in diameter and is composed of roughly 30,000 pieces of Favrile glass, each shaped like a fish scale. Sunlight filters through its translucent surface, shifting blues and golds across its intricate pattern.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ChicagoTiffany_EN-IN9630629960_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ChicagoTiffany_EN-IN9630629960_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":false},"Headline":"Chicago, look up!","Title":"Tiffany Dome, Chicago Cultural Center, Illinois, United States","Copyright":"© Felix Lipov/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/41.88388,-87.62498/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=41.88388,-87.62498;S9;Tiffany Dome, Chicago Cultural Center, Chicago, United States&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260727_ChicagoTiffany\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Tiffany+Dome+Chicago+Cultural+Center&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260726_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260727_ChicagoTiffany"},"Ssd":"20260727","Name":"ChicagoTiffany","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9630629960","FullDateString":"27 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At sunrise in Honduras' Pig Keys—small, low-lying coastal islets tucked within mangrove-rich wetlands—a red mangrove lifts its tangled roots above glassy water. This striking scene captures what 26 July celebrates: the International Day for the Conservation of the Mangrove Ecosystem, created to spotlight these vital coastal forests.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RedMangroveSunrise_EN-IN9234069771_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RedMangroveSunrise_EN-IN9234069771_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Between land and sea, life begins","Title":"Red mangrove in the Pig Keys, Honduras","Copyright":"© Mac Stone/Tandem Stills + Motion","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/14.822356,-86.5979/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=14.822356,-86.5979;S9;Honduras&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260726_RedMangroveSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=International+Day+for+Conservation+of+the+Mangrove+Ecosystem&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260725_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260726_RedMangroveSunrise"},"Ssd":"20260726","Name":"RedMangroveSunrise","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9234069771","FullDateString":"26 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"In Spain's far northwest, Galicia meets the Atlantic with force—its long coastline carved by waves into cliffs, inlets and wave-cut platforms. Rain-fed hills and dense forests spill towards the sea, creating a landscape that feels closer to Ireland than southern Spain, with shifting skies and a distinctly Atlantic mood.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GaliciaBeach_EN-IN8935924229_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GaliciaBeach_EN-IN8935924229_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Into Galicia's hidden arches","Title":"Praia das Catedrais, Galicia, Spain","Copyright":"© Tui De Roy/Amazing Aerial Agency/Abobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.554231,-7.157587/4?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.554231,-7.157587;S9;Praia das Catedrais, Galicia, Spain&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260725_GaliciaBeach\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Galicia+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260724_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260725_GaliciaBeach"},"Ssd":"20260725","Name":"GaliciaBeach","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8935924229","FullDateString":"25 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today is National Cousins Day—a perfect excuse to reconnect with the people who know your family stories best and probably helped create a few of them. Think of cousins as your built-in crew: part family history, part lifelong adventure. The celebration originated in the United States, but some countries have adopted it as a fun way to honour family bonds.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.GalapagosFlamingos_EN-IN8421031392_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.GalapagosFlamingos_EN-IN8421031392_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Family, in full colour","Title":"Flock of American flamingos, Isabela Island, Galápagos Islands, Ecuador","Copyright":"© Tui De Roy/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"Vampire Weekend, the indie rock band, released their single 'Cousins' in 2009.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260724_GalapagosFlamingos\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=National+Cousins+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260723_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260724_GalapagosFlamingos"},"Ssd":"20260724","Name":"GalapagosFlamingos","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8421031392","FullDateString":"24 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Some flowers quietly fill a garden. Dahlias arrive as if they have been cast in the lead role. Native to Mexico, these members of the daisy family come in more than 57,000 cultivated varieties, thanks in part to their unusual genetics. Dahlias are octoploids, meaning they have eight sets of chromosomes, which helps create blooms that range from tiny buttons to 36 centimetres across.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PinkDahlia_EN-IN0092108824_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PinkDahlia_EN-IN0092108824_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A symphony of petals","Title":"Pink dahlia flower","Copyright":"© Harald Biebel/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"One Aztec name for the dahlia, often translated as 'water‑pipe flower,' refers to the plant's long, hollow stems, which were used to transport water.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20260723_PinkDahlia\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Dahlia+genus+plant&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20260722_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20260723_PinkDahlia"},"Ssd":"20260723","Name":"PinkDahlia","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"0092108824","FullDateString":"23 Jul, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Imagine a city built by animals, glowing in the sunlight, and bustling with life beneath the waves. That is a coral reef. During Coral Reef Awareness Week, we celebrate these remarkable ecosystems and the countless species that depend on them.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CoralAwareness_EN-IN9714852805_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CoralAwareness_EN-IN9714852805_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Small footprint, big impact","Title":"Coral reef and beach in Raja Ampat, Indonesia","Copyright":"© SergeUWPhoto/Shutterstock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Ur